    <briefdescription>
<para>Gradient function for the Rectified Linear Unit (<ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1ReLU" kindref="compound">ReLU</ref>) activation function. </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>The <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradReLU" kindref="compound">GradReLU</ref> class represents the <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1ReLU" kindref="compound">ReLU</ref> activation function in the computational graph, computing gradients for the elementwise operation that outputs the maximum of zero and the input. For the operation  <formula id="74">$C =
\text{ReLU}(A) = \max(0, A)$</formula>, the gradient computation follows from the piecewise derivative:      <formula id="75">\[    \frac{\partial C}{\partial A} = \begin{cases}
      1 &amp; \text{if } A &gt; 0 \\
      0 &amp; \text{if } A \leq 0
    \end{cases}
\]</formula></para>
<para>During backpropagation, the incoming gradient  <formula id="8">$\frac{\partial L}{\partial
C}$</formula> is multiplied elementwise with a mask indicating which elements of the input were positive according to the chain rule:      <formula id="76">\[    \frac{\partial L}{\partial A_i} = \begin{cases}
      \frac{\partial L}{\partial C_i} &amp; \text{if } A_i &gt; 0 \\
      0 &amp; \text{if } A_i \leq 0
    \end{cases}
\]</formula></para>
<para>This <ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> saves a backward mask tensor computed during the forward pass, which contains 1 for positive elements and 0 for non-positive elements. The mask is used to efficiently apply the gradient gating during the backward pass without recomputing comparisons.</para>
<para><simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1GradFunction" kindref="compound">GradFunction</ref> for the base class from which this class derives. </para>
</simplesect>
<simplesect kind="see"><para><ref refid="classmattTorch_1_1function_1_1GradTanh" kindref="compound">GradTanh</ref> for the gradient function for the hyperbolic tangent activation. </para>
</simplesect>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
